WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:02.360
Film Courage: When have you been the most
scared in your career?

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:06.589
Dale Stelly, Filmmaker (COMPTON’S FINEST,
SINGLE BLACK FEMALE and more): It’s scary

00:00:06.589 --> 00:00:16.630
when you are dealing with people’s dreams
and stuff and you are not able to make their

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.090
dreams come totally true or what have you.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:23.500
You’re dealing with a lot of dreamers out
here in LA.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.793
My whole thing is I like to help people as
people helped me, you know what I mean?

00:00:29.793 --> 00:00:34.160
But a lot of people dream big and it’s like
sometimes people dream bigger than what they

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.730
can actually accomplish which is nothing wrong
with it but I hate…not hate…but dislike

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:47.170
when you set a goal to work with people or
situations and it doesn’t go in a direction

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:52.309
that you expected and that can be kind of
disheartening sometimes because you put your

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:54.760
heart and energy in productions.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:01:01.700
And it’s just like having a baby and then
certain things can go wrong during the pregnancy.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:05.770
You might break up with the husband or cheated
on you while you are pregnant or something.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:11.640
That’s what I’m saying, like a movie production
things can go wrong like that with a pregnancy

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.440
and the energy is all off.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:18.640
So I like to be part of productions even though
there is no money or little money or whatever

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:22.120
but everyone is positive or sticking to the
goal until we finish.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:29.280
I usually (90% of the time) take on projects
that I know I can actually bring to fruition

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.280
and to life.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:33.820
There are sometimes when you tackle some things
and some things are not meant to be even though

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:39.680
you are putting your whole heart and passion
and resources and running every single play

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.080
that you can to make it a successful production.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:49.610
But some things are not meant to be and I
found out during the course of my career not

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:54.299
everybody is meant to be helped out, you know
what I mean?

00:01:54.299 --> 00:02:01.520
I found out the hard way that sometimes certain
people want to take advantage of you and they

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.659
will say certain things to get you to help
them.

00:02:04.659 --> 00:02:07.700
And once you help them, they flip the script
on you.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.009
And it’s kind of like “Arrghh!”

00:02:10.009 --> 00:02:12.409
I just give everyone the benefit of the doubt.

00:02:12.409 --> 00:02:16.650
And it is always great when a project is green
lit or what have you?

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:21.669
But sometimes people see things that are not
there yet and me I’m always like let’s

00:02:21.669 --> 00:02:26.780
finish the product before you start thinking
about dollars or deals or whatever.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:32.569
But you can’t control people’s expectations
or the way they feel.

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:42.090
And I know these cameras and actors and lights,
it comes with certain expectations.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:47.549
And certain things comes with this territory
that you just have to know how to deal with.

00:02:47.549 --> 00:02:53.949
Film Courage: I had someone I knew who read
Andy Warhol’s biography and this person

00:02:53.949 --> 00:02:59.769
was telling me that certain people loved him
but other people were mad at him because they

00:02:59.769 --> 00:03:03.239
were like “No…you were supposed to make
me famous.”

00:03:03.239 --> 00:03:06.919
Even thought that wasn’t necessarily the
agreement, that’s what they thought.

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:14.059
And so that is a reality of what happens in
this town, whatever you’re doing somebody

00:03:14.059 --> 00:03:20.150
could think “Well you didn’t help me become
famous and I was supposed to become famous.”

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:21.150
Dale: Right.

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:26.970
My thing is I don’t put my career in nobody’s
hands, you know what I mean?

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:33.659
I try to be responsible for my own success.

00:03:33.659 --> 00:03:39.849
When you rely on other people do be successful
that’s not the route to go.

00:03:39.849 --> 00:03:44.709
The road to go is do whatever it takes and
if that’s in yourself and all your hard

00:03:44.709 --> 00:03:50.790
energy and your goals and at the same time
you can help other people with the common

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:58.439
goals and it goes back and forth but it takes
a lot of energy to make this all come to life.

00:03:58.439 --> 00:04:04.450
Film Courage: There is this one quote and
I think it’s from a female musician [Patti

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:08.439
Smyth] and she says just keep your name clean
and good.

00:04:08.439 --> 00:04:13.079
And I think that’s great, a lot of people
have honorable intentions but sometimes you

00:04:13.079 --> 00:04:18.720
can’t help if the other person gets mad
and it’s not something that you did.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:19.720
Dale: Yes, right.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:20.720
Like I said I’m not perfect.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.610
I don’t think anyone is perfect.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:28.880
And everyone goes into situations with a common
goal which is whatever the goal is, let’s

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:29.880
get it done.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:36.750
But with creativity and the creative process
and everyone being individuals and everyone

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:42.639
being responsible for certain things to happen
so other things can happen, some times things

00:04:42.639 --> 00:04:48.840
don’t go right and sometimes people do get
mad and sometimes people do not understand

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:55.009
what you were doing for them in the beginning.

00:04:55.009 --> 00:04:57.430
It can turn into a headache, things can turn
into headache.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:03.330
But my thing is what puts away the headaches
at the end of the day is when the product

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:08.200
eventually gets completed and it comes out,
you know what I mean?

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:16.550
I’ve been on productions a couple of times
where people wanted to hurt people and stuff.

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:20.370
And at the end of the day when the movie comes
out and everything and it came out through

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:26.460
Sony and the way it was supposed to, people
forgot about the arguments and wanting to

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:29.409
fight on set and things of that nature.

00:05:29.409 --> 00:05:40.280
But nothing is perfect and that’s why I
stay prayed-up as much as I can and pray for

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:46.590
successful situations even if it goes wrong,
figure out how to get it back on track and

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:54.110
I don’t like to be part of negative situations
because it’s already hard enough whatever

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:55.190
the goal is already.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:59.530
If it wasn’t hard it would already be done
or it would already be financed or it would

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:06.590
already be done with (with a bigger situation)
so to me I’m always like an underdog compared

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:08.180
to these other studios.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:13.629
I know exactly what to do and these other
studios and everything but I don’t have

00:06:13.629 --> 00:06:17.120
the manpower or the money behind me.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:23.069
It might take me longer to figure it out but
I can eventually figure out whatever the goal

00:06:23.069 --> 00:06:24.069
is or task is.

00:06:24.069 --> 00:06:25.720
It’s just a matter of time.

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:30.530
In this business, money pays for things to
get done faster, you know what I mean?

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:36.520
So on that note, it’s knowing how to use
your time and money effectively and everything

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:37.739
eventually gets done.

